6. Reference BLAS and BLAS test programs (refblas/, test/F77/, test/C/)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

- refblas/*.f except xerbla.f: the reference implementation of the BLAS as
  distributed with LAPACK 3.3.1 (BLAS/SRC of lapack-3.3.1.tgz,
  https://www.netlib.org/lapack/), unmodified.
- refblas/xerbla.f: XERBLA of the reference BLAS from Netlib
  (https://www.netlib.org/blas/).
- test/F77/: the BLAS test programs from Netlib (xblat1, xblat2, xblat3),
  adapted for the test suite of ulmBLAS; the input files *.dat.in are
  derived from the Netlib input files.  test/F77/sblat1.f and
  test/F77/dblat1.f are the test programs of LAPACK 3.12.1
  (BLAS/TESTING of https://github.com/Reference-LAPACK/lapack, tag
  v3.12.1), unmodified.  test/F77/ublat1.f belongs to ulmBLAS.
- ulmblas/level1/rot.tcc: rotm and rotmg implement the algorithms of
  SROTM/DROTM and SROTMG/DROTMG of the reference BLAS (LAPACK 3.12.1, with
  the correction of the rescaling in SROTMG/DROTMG of the Reference-LAPACK
  development version, commit 6a1a8b8a), rewritten in C++.
- test/C/: the CBLAS test programs from Netlib (cblas.tgz,
  https://www.netlib.org/blas/blast-forum/), adapted for the test suite of
  ulmBLAS.

The changes made by ulmBLAS are recorded in the Git history.
refblas/Makefile belongs to ulmBLAS.

Netlib states the following terms for the reference BLAS
(https://www.netlib.org/blas/faq.html):

  The reference BLAS is a freely-available software package.  It is
  available from netlib via anonymous ftp and the World Wide Web.  Thus,
  it can be included in commercial software packages (and has been).  We
  only ask that proper credit be given to the authors.

  Like all software, it is copyrighted.  It is not trademarked, but we do
  ask the following:

  If you modify the source for these routines we ask that you change the
  name of the routine and comment the changes made to the original.

  We will gladly answer any questions regarding the software.  If a
  modification is done, however, it is the responsibility of the person
  who modified the routine to provide support.

The license of LAPACK 3.3.1 (file LICENSE of lapack-3.3.1.tgz, verbatim).
LAPACK 3.12.1 has the same license with the following copyright notice:

  Copyright (c) 1992-2023 The University of Tennessee and The University
